    const res = await fetch("/api/weather");
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
    const data = await res.json();
    cityEl.textContent = data.city;
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
  }
}

lessons.theory:
If the user clicks the button twice before the first fetch finishes, two requests run in parallel. Prevent this by disabling the button at the start and re-enabling it at the end:

```javascript
async function loadWeather() {
  loadBtn.disabled = true;
  try {
    // ... fetch logic ...
  } finally {
    loadBtn.disabled = false;
  }
}
```

`finally` always runs, whether `try` succeeded or `catch` caught an error. This ensures the button is always re-enabled, even after a failure.

