lessons.theory:
Good UX tells the user something is happening. Set placeholder text before the fetch and replace it with real content when it arrives:

```javascript
cityEl.textContent = "Loading...";
descEl.textContent = "";
tempEl.textContent = "";
loadBtn.disabled = true;
try {
  // fetch ...
```

This is called **optimistic UI feedback**. The user sees the page react immediately, even if the network takes a second.

The same principle applies to spinners, progress bars and skeleton screens: show something the moment the user acts.

