lessons.theory:
APIs often return arrays. To display them, create one element per item and append it:

```javascript
const list = document.querySelector("#results");
list.innerHTML = ""; // clear old items
data.items.forEach(item => {
  const li = document.createElement("li");
  li.textContent = item.name;
  list.appendChild(li);
});
```

Clearing `innerHTML` before appending avoids duplicates when the user clicks the button more than once.

For larger lists, build all elements first into a `DocumentFragment`, then append the fragment in one operation. That is faster because it causes only one browser reflow.

lessons.starter:
const list = document.querySelector("#list");
